  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 235 PM MDT THU AUG 13 2026\nA ridge of high pressure will build back into the region on Sunday, \nbringing warm and mostly dry conditions to the area. Lingering \nmoisture aloft will keep a slight chance of showers and \nthunderstorms over high terrain in the central Idaho mountains. A \nquick moving trough will bring cooler air with increased chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms on Tuesday into early Wednesday. \nConfidence in the forecast after Wednesday decreases thanks to \nincreased model variability. Significant disagreement exists in the \nlong term, with some model solutions showing a trough through the \nnorthwest towards the end of the week while other models depict a \nridge of high pressure building back in over the Intermountain West \nthrough the end of the week. If the trough slows over our region, \ncooler and wetter conditions will occur, but expect very hot and dry \nand conditions if the ridge builds quickly back into the area. \nCurrent forecasts favor the ridge building quickly back in, with a \nhigher probability of warm and dry conditions continuing through the \nend of the week.",
